    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e9ce938d193452c8e54a8687ce32437c8fb0083cbbd45fba199c5e0fb92b94c4",
      "text": "Day 7 · City tour (3 hours) with an English-speaking guide, through a capital of elegant architecture, museums, galleries and theatres. Explore the colourful district of La Boca and historic San Telmo, with its bars, restaurants and the antiques market on Plaza Dorrego, then Plaza de Mayo, the heart of the city, with the Casa Rosada, the presidential palace associated with Evita Perón.\n\nSee the 67-metre Obelisk, symbol of the city, and the elegant Recoleta district with its famous cemetery and the colonial-style church of El Pilar, before discovering modern Puerto Madero, Parque Lezama and the Tres de Febrero parks.\n\nEvening · Tango show with dinner. Born in the port neighbourhoods of Buenos Aires among immigrants and working people, tango has become one of the most sensual dances in the world. On stage, its passion and virtuosity take you into a world of love and grace, while a menu of traditional dishes with excellent Argentine wines completes this romantic evening.",
